# mente-pause — stop the checks without losing anything

🔴 **THE FAILURE THIS ANSWERS, measured 2026-09-07.** `bin/off` and `bin/on`
shipped and never appeared in the `/` menu, so nobody knew the system could be
paused. ⛔ A guard with no visible way out is one people work around instead of
switching off honestly — and a worked-around guard leaves no trace.

## To pause

```bash
Mente/bin/off
```

⭐ **Say what it means, in their words:** *"the checks stop running. Nothing is
deleted — your files, your work and your notes are exactly as they were."*

## To resume

```bash
Mente/bin/on
```

## ⚠️ Before you pause

⛔ **Ask why.** ⭐ A gate refusing something is usually right, and pausing it to
get past one refusal is how a protection quietly ends.

| They want to | ⭐ Do this instead |
|---|---|
| write one throwaway file | `MENTE_SCRATCH=1` on that one command |
| work outside the open block | ask if the block's boundary should widen — ⛔ and let THEM decide |
| get past a refusal they disagree with | ⚠️ read the refusal out loud first · it names the way forward |

⭐ **Pausing is legitimate** — a demo, a migration, a day of throwaway work. ⛔
Pausing to avoid one specific refusal is not, and saying so is part of the job.

## ⬜ Where a path lives

⛔ **Do not hardcode a path from another installation.** ⭐ Every engine piece is
listed in `Mente/pieces.tsv` — read it when you need to know where something is,
and a moved piece stays findable without editing this file.
